steps.prompt_template:
You are executing one task of a refactor. The approved plan [attached — from s-analyse] has been broken into an ordered task list, and you have exactly one task from it.

## Your task ({{task_index}} of {{task_total}}): {{task_title}}
{{task_description}}

Files you are expected to touch: {{task_files}}

## Already done (committed on your branch by earlier agents)
{{completed_tasks}}

The worktree already contains the committed work above. Read it and build on it rather than redoing or reverting it.

## Constraints
- Structure changes, observable behaviour does not. The plan's Behaviour Invariants hold for every file you touch.
- The tree compiles and the tests pass when you finish: {{test_command}}. Your task is a checkpoint the next agent builds on, so a broken tree blocks everyone after you.

{{retry_feedback_section}}

## Reply
- What you restructured, and why it is behaviour-preserving
- Test results (pass/fail counts)
- `## Handoff` — what the next task's agent needs to know, or `none`. This section is carried into the next task's prompt; nothing else in your reply is.
